The first route in 29's list: immediate, no gatekeeping, works on Linux as
well as macOS, and the formula is about ten lines ending in
bin.install "bin/pidly".

Needs a version and a release tarball with a checksum first, so it waits on
the version ticket. Needs a second repository — homebrew-pidly — which is a
publishing decision for the owner.

Blocked in practice on 41 as well: the formula would serve macOS, and until
the suite has been run on a real BSD find nobody knows pidly works there.

Done when a clean macOS machine and a clean Linux one can brew install it
from the tap and run pidly init in a fresh repo.
